# Build context exclusions (Phase 8.1). Patterns are relative to the context root, so a bare
# `docs` means the one at the top, unlike .gitignore where it would also match src/docs/.
#
# **The .env lines are the load-bearing ones.** Coolify builds from a git clone, where .env was
# never committed — but a *local* `docker build` (T2.4's proof) sends the working directory to the
# daemon, and a copied .env would be baked into an image layer, secrets and all, and would then
# silently shadow the environment Coolify supplies at runtime. Both halves are bad; neither is
# visible from the outside.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Never rebuilt from, always regenerated inside the image. `node_modules` is also the single
# biggest thing in this directory, and shipping the Mac's arm64 tree to an amd64 build would be
# actively wrong, not just slow.
node_modules
.next
.cache
.playwright
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# .git is excluded on purpose and the serwist route knows it: the precache revision reads
# SOURCE_COMMIT first because `git rev-parse` cannot work in here.
.git
.github
.claude
.superpowers

# Not needed at runtime, and leaving them out keeps a rebuild from being invalidated every time a
# walkthrough, a log entry or a spec is edited — the files that change most often in this repo.
docs
e2e
*.md
!README.md

# Phase 0's throwaway harnesses and tooling. Nothing at runtime reads them: the topic graph the
# feed walks is checked in at src/server/config/topic-graph.json.
phase0

*.zip
start-database.sh
.DS_Store
